From 0b97b6f65b3cc1318acaeb1e3fef11bf1ea754de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri John Ledkov <dimitri.ledkov@surgut.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:24:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Port to current OpenSSL APIs

Build against OpenSSL 4.0, which makes ASN1_STRING opaque, returns
const pointers from more X509 accessors, and removes long-deprecated
functions.

* Access ASN1_STRING contents through ASN1_STRING_type(),
  ASN1_STRING_get0_data(), and ASN1_STRING_length().
* Use X509_get_ext_d2i() to fetch subjectAltName extensions instead of
  X509_get_ext() and X509V3_EXT_d2i().
* Treat the X509_NAME values returned by X509_get_subject_name() and
  X509_get_issuer_name() as const.
* Replace X509_STORE_CTX_trusted_stack() with
  X509_STORE_CTX_set0_trusted_stack().
* Replace the deprecated X509_NAME_get_text_by_NID() in k5tls.
* Remove calls to SSL_library_init(), SSL_load_error_strings(),
  ERR_load_crypto_strings(), and OpenSSL_add_all_algorithms(); OpenSSL
  has initialized itself since 1.1.0.
* Regenerate the PKCS#12 test bundles without -descert, and the
  encrypted test private key with -aes256 instead of -des3, so that the
  test fixtures use AES rather than triple DES.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
